ont-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"0.0023\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.0023</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>). The mean of stack loss is not a\nfunction of air flow alone, which points to the other operating\nvariables, taken up in <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"exm-cor-stackloss-full\">@exm-cor-stackloss-full</span>.</p>","file":"ch14-correlation-lack-of-fit-prediction/06-lack-of-fit.html"}